136bb56c0fecbe1561f1288c5fb6aae71dd7402a23","event_uuid":"259d884d-ef14-4044-9dca-95f70b60454d","position":{"commit_sha":"31c8d6e760986c29af9ab4492b03beb916fb38cd","position":"1793801940947125001-259d884d-ef14-4044-9dca-95f70b60454d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"81fca821a49cbd3b81a9f6e05162099f850d00b12ea7f77d221b85b914530859","event_uuid":"5aff3db3-2c0a-4cee-a987-e414e0c5b958","position":{"commit_sha":"0ad5be9161b8ad42f550e11c791f3acebd7c9dd3","position":"1793801956384730001-5aff3db3-2c0a-4cee-a987-e414e0c5b958"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Failing branch identified (AC 1). Evidence, 2026-11-04 PST, worktree fix-bunting at fe6c2100292:\n\n- The test's git stub writes the `rev-parse-seen` barrier BEFORE it checks `head-resolves`. A scratch copy of the module with `sleep 1` between those two lines fails the peer-finishing test 5 of 5 runs (each ~1.6-1.8 s) with the CI signature: stderr is only `mcp: tickets store provisioning finished`, rc 0.\n- Recorded git call sequence for the failing run: `config --global ...helper`, `config --global ...useHttpPath false`, `rev-parse --verify -q HEAD` (once), `clone --filter=blob:none --single-branch --branch main ...` (code side). No second rev-parse and no `--branch tickets` clone.\n- Interpretation of that sequence: the first, unlocked probe in `provision_store` saw a healthy store (the peer's touch landed inside the stub's window), so the script never entered `reclone_store`. That is correct script behaviour; the defect is the test's barrier ordering.\n- The unmodified scratch copy passes. With the stub reordered (decide, write marker, then the same 1 s stall, then exit) the whole module passes 5 of 5 (~59 s each, because the stall applies to every rev-parse in that scratch copy).","timestamp":1793797951228702001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Determinism evidence (AC 2), 2026-11-04 PST, worktree fix-bunting:\n- Stall hook + `probe_stall=True` with the OLD stub ordering (signal, stall, decide): `pytest -k peer_finishing` failed 5 of 5 runs, each with `AssertionError: the lock holder must re-probe HEAD before re-cloning: mcp: tickets store provisioning finished`.\n- Fixed ordering (decide, signal, stall, exit): 5 of 5 passed.\n- Module set (AC 3, local half): test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py, tests/infra/test_mcp_entrypoint.py, test_mcp_on_box_infra.py, test_check_deploy_manifest.py, tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py: 193 passed. make lint and make typecheck: exit 0.\n- infra/scripts/mcp-entrypoint.sh unchanged (AC 4). Pushed as Gerrit change 3302, commit ea4fb8b641f.","timestamp":1793798926918562001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed: Gerrit change 3302 merged at 2026-11-04 05:59 PST as ea4fb8b641f266eedc932a60c626598597ef2dcb (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1 on that revision; the Verified CI run covered the full default test tier including this module). infra/scripts/mcp-entrypoint.sh is unchanged, so no MCP autodeploy is triggered.","timestamp":1793800847412409001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1793782758672096001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"acd1ebb8-337b-4923-83e3-38c790cadada","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"fb16-a8b0-c2b7-449a"},{"link_uuid":"46941c96-ec2e-4f07-b264-d751dbd6d6a8","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b1a3-3e62-f1ff-4748"},{"link_uuid":"6ef933cf-a308-4650-bf0a-a59031313841","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"cfa8-e54c-66c0-4391"},{"link_uuid":"5aff3db3-2c0a-4cee-a987-e414e0c5b958","provenance":"derived","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"d467-e2fc-fd64-49ae"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py::test_a_peer_finishing_the_clone_while_we_wait_skips_the_redundant_reclone` failed in `make verify` on 2026-11-04 PST (worktree fix-caudata, commit `ff107f59ce2`) with `AssertionError: the lock holder must re-probe HEAD before re-cloning`. Script stderr held only `mcp: tickets store provisioning finished`, returncode 0. It passed 10 of 10 runs alone at load average 31. `stellar-sane-hawk` (closed) recorded the same test failing once; its stated cause (a pytest-timeout crashing the worker in `test_review_bot.py`) cannot produce this assertion.\n\n## Root cause (reproduced)\nThe defect is in the test's git stub, not in `infra/scripts/mcp-entrypoint.sh`. The stub's `rev-parse` branch writes the barrier marker `rev-parse-seen` BEFORE it checks `head-resolves`. The test's peer callback waits for that marker, then touches `head-resolves` and releases the lock. If the stub is descheduled between its marker write and its `head-resolves` check (host load), the peer's touch lands first, the script's FIRST probe (`provision_store`, before any lock) reports a healthy store, and the script correctly skips `reclone_store` entirely. So no re-probe and no `was re-cloned by another container` line, rc 0: exactly the observed signature.\n\nEvidence: a scratch copy of the module with `sleep 1` inserted between the marker write and the `head-resolves` check fails 5 of 5 runs with the identical stderr and rc 0; the recorded git calls are `config`, `config`, one `rev-parse --verify -q HEAD`, then only the code-side `clone --branch main` (no tickets clone, no second rev-parse). The unmodified copy passes. With the stub reordered (decide, then write the marker) and the same 1 s stall placed AFTER the marker, the whole module passes 5 of 5.\n\nThe script's behaviour is correct for production: when the first probe sees a healthy store it has no reason to lock or re-clone. Real `git rev-parse` has no barrier side channel, so there is no production analogue of this race.\n\n## Approach\nFix the class \"a barrier marker signals before the state it reports is sampled\": in `_GIT_STUB`'s `rev-parse` branch, compute the exit status from `head-resolves` first, then append `rev-parse-seen`, then exit with the computed status. The marker then announces a probe whose answer is already fixed, so no peer action after the marker can change that probe's outcome.\n\nMake the test deterministic against regression by adding an optional stall to the stub: when the state marker `rev-parse-stall` exists, the stub sleeps 1 s after writing the barrier marker (standing in for a descheduled stub under load). `_provision` gains a `probe_stall: bool = False` keyword that creates that marker alongside the existing ones, and the peer-finishing test passes `probe_stall=True`. With the old ordering this test fails every run; with the new ordering it passes every run. The re-probe assertion (`was re-cloned by another container`) and the no-tickets-clone assertion stay unchanged. No autouse fixtures; the child process still starts through `_subprocess_env.subprocess_env`. No change to `infra/scripts/mcp-entrypoint.sh`.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py`: reorder the stub's `rev-parse` branch; add the `rev-parse-stall` hook; add the `probe_stall` keyword to `_provision`; pass `probe_stall=True` in the peer-finishing test; update the comments on the barrier.\n\n## Testing\n- Red first: commit-order check in the worktree. Apply the stall hook and `probe_stall=True` with the OLD stub ordering and run the peer-finishing test 5 times: expect 5 failures with the original assertion. Then reorder: expect 5 passes.\n- Run the whole module plus the other entrypoint and infra modules that exercise `mcp-entrypoint.sh`: `tests/infra/test_mcp_entrypoint.py`, `tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py`, `tests/unit/test_check_deploy_manifest.py`, `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py`, with the worktree `.venv/bin` first on PATH.\n- `make lint` and `make typecheck`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The failing branch is identified with recorded evidence (git call sequence and timing) in a comment on this ticket.\n- [x] The peer-finishing test is deterministic regardless of host load without weakening the re-probe assertion: with the stall hook enabled it fails 5 of 5 runs under the old stub ordering and passes 5 of 5 under the fixed ordering, recorded in a comment on this ticket.\n- [x] The full `test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py` module passes locally, and the change's CI `Verified +1` run (which runs the full default test tier) passes it.\n- [x] `infra/scripts/mcp-entrypoint.sh` is unchanged.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py","reason":"reorder the git stub barrier and add the deterministic post-signal stall"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","b1a3-3e62-f1ff-4748"],["relates_to","cfa8-e54c-66c0-4391"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"a11eae8a-57e5-4f2b-9564-c37ac853ea28","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"5618-ebca-c29f-47c0","ticket_type":"bug","title":"MCP entrypoint peer-finished-clone test misses the re-probe message under a loaded make verify","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c268012c-ae47-4471-ae30-caf78956db80","90d3f3fe-981d-473d-8d12-fea4ea731c08","f07988a1-2c56-4566-ab97-1b9ec2de61e9","b059706a-7b8a-4670-a817-cd12149f0801","f01811ac-b7a4-4958-9d48-a6e87f864a4c","ecd71c92-f1d2-422e-95c2-7695fdff2127","224928f2-5ce0-4bdc-ac2d-980bee94363e","6ef933cf-a308-4650-bf0a-a59031313841","b88f9a9d-1ba6-46c0-9856-e809817fc437","37a6b083-5b98-40ce-a484-7f7633847b45","69b62f26-171f-4cb6-9f8c-bd71b9167ae4","a11eae8a-57e5-4f2b-9564-c37ac853ea28","259d884d-ef14-4044-9dca-95f70b60454d","5aff3db3-2c0a-4cee-a987-e414e0c5b958"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793801956384730002,"uuid":"cabe8e62-a8ec-4e0d-b9c4-a6c0215c0afe"}